    # Circuit breaker for calls to the Semantic Processing Service (e.g., for detailed NLP)
    semanticProcessingServiceBreaker:
      registerHealthIndicator: true
      slidingWindowType: COUNT_BASED
      slidingWindowSize: 100 # Evaluate last 100 calls
      minimumNumberOfCalls: 10 # Minimum calls before calculating failure rate
      failureRateThreshold: 60 # If 60% of calls fail, open the circuit
      waitDurationInOpenState: 30s # Stay open for 30 seconds
      permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState: 5 # Allow 5 calls in half-open state to test recovery
      automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled: true

    # Circuit breaker for calls to a Context Management Service
    contextManagementServiceBreaker:
      registerHealthIndicator: true
      slidingWindowType: TIME_BASED
      slidingWindowSize: 60 # Evaluate calls in the last 60 seconds
      minimumNumberOfCalls: 20
      failureRateThreshold: 75
      waitDurationInOpenState: 60s
      permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState: 10
      automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled: true
```
This configuration defines two distinct circuit breakers, each tailored to the expected behavior and criticality of the service it protects. The `semanticProcessingServiceBreaker` uses a count-based window, suitable for services where a quick assessment of recent failures is needed. The `contextManagementServiceBreaker` uses a time-based window, which might be more appropriate for services with varying call rates.

